  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.2/rooms/v9/#definitions\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\n> Given an m.room.power_levels event P, the mainline of P is the list of events generated by starting with P and recursively taking the m.room.power_levels events from the auth_events, ordered such that P is last.\r\n\r\nThere are two ways to interpret `recursively taking the m.room.power_levels events from the auth_events`.\r\n\r\n1. Start with P0. Retrieve P1, the power level event in P0's auth events. Retrieve P2, the power level event in P1's auth events. Continue to retrieve P_i until you reach an event with no power level auth event. The mainline of P is the list `[P_n, P_{n-1}, ..., P_2, P_1, P_0]` of all power events found.\r\n\r\n2. Start with P0 and compute its auth chain C. The mainline of P is the set { power level events in A's auth events | A is in C }... ordered... somehow.\r\n\r\nOn first reading this, I thought definition (2) was intended (and Rich concurred, but then wasn't sure).  @erikjohnston confirms that (1) is intended.\r\n",
